## Trace: HashedLink usage-based expiration

**Migration column & default**
Migration `20250707145503_add_private_links_expiration_capability` (`packages/prisma/migrations/.../migration.sql`) adds three columns to `HashedLink`, including `maxUsageCount INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1`. The Prisma schema mirrors this: `maxUsageCount Int @default(1)` (`packages/prisma/schema.prisma:1252`), alongside `usageCount Int @default(0)` and the older `expiresAt DateTime?` (time-based expiry).

**`isUsageBasedExpired` boundary condition**
In `packages/lib/hashedLinksUtils.ts:93-96`:
```ts
export function isUsageBasedExpired(usageCount: number, maxUsageCount?: number | null): boolean {
  if (!maxUsageCount || maxUsageCount <= 0) return false;
  return usageCount >= maxUsageCount;
}
```
The link is considered exhausted when `usageCount >= maxUsageCount` (i.e. once usage count reaches the cap, not only when it exceeds it) — the boundary is inclusive (`>=`), not strictly `>`.

**Order of checks in `validateHashedLinkData`**
`packages/lib/hashedLinksUtils.ts:103-111` checks **time-based expiration first**:
```ts
export function validateHashedLinkData(linkData: HashedLinkData): void {
  if (isTimeBasedExpired(linkData.expiresAt, linkData.eventType)) {
    throw new Error(ErrorCode.PrivateLinkExpired);
  }
  if (isUsageBasedExpired(linkData.usageCount, linkData.maxUsageCount)) {
    throw new Error(ErrorCode.PrivateLinkExpired);
  }
}
```
`isTimeBasedExpired` runs before `isUsageBasedExpired`.

**Error code**
Both branches throw `ErrorCode.PrivateLinkExpired`, defined in `packages/lib/errorCodes.ts:39` as:
```ts
PrivateLinkExpired = "private_link_expired",
```
This single code identifies both an expired (time-based) and an exhausted (usage-based) private link — the two cases aren't distinguished by error code.

**v2 API schema corroboration**
`packages/platform/types/event-types/inputs/private-link.input.ts` (`CreatePrivateLinkInput.maxUsageCount`) documents:
> "Maximum number of times the link can be used. If omitted and expiresAt is not provided, defaults to 1 (one time use)."
with Swagger metadata `default: 1, minimum: 1`. This matches the Prisma/migration default of `1`.
